    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-01T09:16:37+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-01T09:16:37+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T23:46:37Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-31T23:46:37Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front is expected to move across SA today as a high pressure system moves further east of Australia. Another high pressure ridge will move across the north of the state on Wednesday and Thursday and another cold front will slip across the southeast of SA early Thursday. The ridge will move eastwards early Friday then another trough and cold front will move over SA during the day.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW002" description="Yorke Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-01T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-31T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northwesterly 25 to 40 km/h turning west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low 20s.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 2:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 6 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. Winds southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light before dawn then becoming westerly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 9 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers in the south, medium chance elsewhere. Winds west to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Light winds becoming northerly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending northwesterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
